==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-big gun.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|military}} A large [[artillery]] gun or one of the largest-caliber [[naval]] guns (as on a [[battleship]]).
#: {{syn|en|great gun}}
#* '''1870''' Dec. 2, "[http://paperspast.natlib.govt.nz/cgi-bin/paperspast?a=d&d=ST18701202.2.11 The Suez Mail]," ''Southland Times'' (New Zealand), Issue 1342, p. 2:
#*: London, Nov. 1: The '''big guns''' opened fire on Paris today at mid-day.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=March 26 1968|titleurl=http://news.google.com/newspapers?id=tSFgAAAAIBAJ&sjid=ZG4NAAAAIBAJ&pg=3437,4076814&dq=her-big-guns+battleship&hl=en|title=Battleship begins Viet Tests|journal=Evening News|location=Newburgh, NY, USA|page=1|accessdate=19 Aug 2011
|passage=The smaller crew was possible because the battleship was stripped of all but her '''big guns'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=Dec 6 2008|author=[[w:William J. Bennett|William J. Bennett]]|author2=John Cribb|title=Deadly resolve answered attack|titleurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20110812195412/http://www.dcourier.com/main.asp?SectionID=36|journal=Daily Courier|accessdate=19 Aug. 2011|location=USA
|passage=The USS West Virginia became one of many symbols of American resolve. . . . Her '''big guns''' pounded the enemy at the battles of Leyte Gulf, Iwo Jima, and Okinawa.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|by extension|usually [[pluralize]]d}} A person, group, thing, or course of action that is [[powerful]], [[influential]], or particularly [[effective]].
#: {{syn|en|big shot|bigwig|Thesaurus:important person}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=June 6 1888|title=A Great Day for Big Guns|titleurl=http://select.nytimes.com/gst/abstract.html?res=F30816F93C5E1A738DDDAE0894DE405B8884F0D3|journal=New York Times|accessdate=20 Aug. 2011
|passage=This has been a great day for the big guns. This does not refer to Prof. Lummis and the other '''big guns''' of the Board of Visitors, for every day is a great one for them.}}
#* '''1957''' Aug. 28, Ed Wilks, "[http://news.google.com/newspapers?id=BgkeAAAAIBAJ&sjid=30UEAAAAIBAJ&pg=6689,5400266&dq=big-gun&hl=en Sports]" (Headline), ''Park City News'' (USA), p. 15 <small>(retrieved 20 Aug. 2011)</small>:
#*: Berra Is '''Big Gun''' In Yankee Victory
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=June 29 2001|author=Frank Pellegrini|title=Whatever Happened to Military Restructuring?|titleurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120109133353/http://www.time.com/time/nation/article/0,8599,165668,00.html|journal=Time
|passage=And the administration's '''big guns''' — Bush, Cheney, Powell and once-and-current Defense Secretary Donald Rumsfeld — had the clout to make bold and necessary changes.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=March 26 2007|author=Yuri Wuensch|title=Eric Clapton simply masterful|titleurl=http://jam.canoe.ca/Music/Artists/C/Clapton_Eric/ConcertReviews/2007/03/26/3835986.html|journal=canoe.ca|accessdate=20 Aug. 2011|location=Canada
|passage=Clapton kept the '''big guns''' for last, finishing the set off with Derek and the Domino's "Layla", complete with the haunting instrumentals at song's end.}}

